  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The VRChat platform is largely sustained by content created by the community itself. Worlds, experiences, and events are developed by creators who invest time, knowledge, and resources to keep the platform alive and constantly evolving. For this reason, transparency about fundamental platform systems, such as the world search system, is extremely important.\n\nCurrently, there is no clear explanation or public documentation about how the search system organizes or prioritizes worlds in the results. This makes it difficult for creators to understand how to improve their projects, optimize names, descriptions, or tags, and reach the right audience.\n\nThis lack of information can also create a sense of inconsistency or unfairness, since worlds with little activity or no recent updates sometimes appear before active projects that receive frequent updates and maintain engaged players. Without any guidance about which factors influence ranking, creators are left trying to guess how the system works.\n\nProviding at least general guidelines on how the search system considers factors such as world activity, number of players, updates, tags, or other criteria would greatly help creators develop better and more relevant experiences for the community.\n\nGreater transparency in this area would benefit not only creators but also platform users, who would be able to find higher quality content more easily. Since the community is a central part of the VRChat ecosystem, providing this type of guidance would further strengthen the platform’s growth and quality.",
